IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `qld-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `qld-part05-commencement`
IMPORT `qld-part06-amendment-and-repeal`
IMPORT `qld-part10-service-of-documents`
IMPORT `qld-part12a-forms`
IMPORT `qld-part12b-fee-units`
IMPORT `qld-part13-miscellaneous`
IMPORT `qld-schedule1-terms`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has a time limit to meet under a Queensland Act or statutory instrument (to apply, object,
-- appeal, reply or pay), or who needs to know when something takes effect, asking on which day their period ends
-- and which of their days count.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask:
-- on which day does my time run out, which days count, when does a law start or stop, when is my posted letter taken
-- to have arrived, how old am I for the Act's purposes, and what does a fee in fee units come to.  Nothing here is new law.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs: yes/no, numbers, dates, lists of dates, and the modules' own
-- choices, one for each fact the person can state, each with a @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- Every rule is called from the module that encodes it; no rule is restated here.  The only things built in this file
-- are the records the modules ask for (a length of a period, the facts about the days of a place), made from the answers.
--
-- Facts the Act leaves to other instruments are asked: the public holidays, special holidays and bank holidays of the
-- place where the person must act (Schedule 1, "public holiday", "business day"), the days an office is closed
-- (s 38(5)(a)), the value of a fee unit (s 48B), and the time at which a letter would be delivered in the ordinary
-- course of post (s 39A(1)(b)).
--
-- A period of weeks is not answered: the Act does not define "week" (see the time module).
-- A period of years is read as twelve calendar months for each year (NOTES.md, fork register).

§ `Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Queensland) -- the questions of a person who has a time to meet`

§§ `Fixtures built from the answers`

-- The days that do not count are those on which the office is closed (for filing or registering a document, s 38(5)(a)),
-- and otherwise the days that are not business days (s 38(5)(b)): Saturdays, Sundays and the holidays of the place.
GIVEN closed IS A LIST OF DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `Facts about the days of a place`
`the facts about my days` MEANS `Facts about the days of a place` WITH
    `the days on which the office is closed where the filing or registration must or may be done` IS closed
    `the public holidays, special holidays and bank holidays in the place where the thing must or may be done` IS holidays

GIVEN filing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Purpose of the time`
`my purpose` MEANS
    IF filing
    THEN `filing or registering a document`
    ELSE `anything other than filing or registering a document`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Length of a period`
`my period of days` MEANS `Length of a period` WITH `how many` IS n, `in what unit` IS `a number of days`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Length of a period`
`my period of months` MEANS `Length of a period` WITH `how many` IS n, `in what unit` IS `a number of calendar months`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Length of a period`
`my period of years` MEANS `Length of a period` WITH `how many` IS n, `in what unit` IS `a number of years`

§§ `When a law takes effect, and when it stops (Parts 5 and 6)`

-- s 15A.  An Act commences on the date of assent except so far as the Act otherwise expressly provides.
-- When the Act does otherwise expressly provide, this section does not say when it starts: NOTHING.
@export On which day does an Act take effect if it says nothing different about its start (s 15A)?
GIVEN `the date of assent` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Act receive the royal assent?
      `the Act says expressly when it starts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act itself say, in so many words, a different time at which it starts?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does an Act take effect if it says nothing different about its start` IS
    `the day an Act commences on the date of assent (s 15A)` `the date of assent` `the Act says expressly when it starts`

-- s 15D.  A day fixed by proclamation that comes before the day the proclamation is notified: the Act or provision
-- commences on the notification day.
@export On which day does an Act take effect when its start is fixed by proclamation (s 15D)?
GIVEN `the day fixed by the proclamation` IS A DATE @desc Which day does the proclamation fix for the Act or provision to start?
      `the day the proclamation was notified` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the proclamation notified?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does an Act take effect when its start is fixed by proclamation` IS
    `the day an Act commences when a day is fixed by proclamation (s 15D)` `the day fixed by the proclamation` `the day the proclamation was notified`

-- s 15DA.  A postponed law that has not commenced within 1 year of the assent day commences automatically on the next day;
-- a regulation made within that year may extend the period to not more than 2 years.
@export On which day does an Act whose start was left to a proclamation start by itself (s 15DA)?
GIVEN `the assent day` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the Act that postponed the start receive the royal assent?
      `the Act says expressly that section 15DA does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act say, in so many words, that section 15DA of the Acts Interpretation Act 1954 does not apply?
      `the months to which a regulation extended the period` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many months after the assent day did a regulation extend the period before the start? (0 if no regulation extended it)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does an Act whose start was left to a proclamation start by itself` IS
    `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)` `the assent day` `the Act says expressly that section 15DA does not apply` `the months to which a regulation extended the period`

-- s 17(3) and (4).  A thing done before the enabling provision commences (an instrument or an appointment) takes effect
-- on the day it is made, or on the day the enabling provision commences, unless it is expressed to take effect at a later time.
@export On which day does an instrument or appointment made before its enabling law starts take effect (s 17)?
GIVEN `it is an appointment, or an instrument or provision that is not necessary for the power to be exercised or brought into effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an appointment, or an instrument (or part of one) that is not needed for the power under the new law to be exercised or brought into effect?
      `the day it was made` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the instrument made?
      `the day the enabling provision commences` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the provision that gives the power commence?
      `it says it takes effect at a later time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it say that it takes effect at a later time?
      `the later day it names` IS A DATE @desc Which day does it name for taking effect? (any day if it names none)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does an instrument or appointment made before its enabling law starts take effect` IS
    IF `it is an appointment, or an instrument or provision that is not necessary for the power to be exercised or brought into effect`
    THEN `the day an appointment, or an instrument or provision not necessary under s 17(3), takes effect (s 17(4))` `the day the enabling provision commences` `the day it names, if it names one`
    ELSE `the day an instrument or provision necessary under s 17(3) takes effect (s 17(3))` `the day it was made` `the day it names, if it names one`
    WHERE
        `the day it names, if it names one` MEANS
            IF `it says it takes effect at a later time` THEN JUST `the later day it names` ELSE NOTHING

-- s 15B.  A provision that commences on a day commences at the beginning of the day, so it is in force at the beginning of that day.
@export Is a law already in force at the beginning of a given day (s 15B)?
GIVEN `the day the law commences` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the Act or provision commence?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a law already in force at the beginning of a given day` IF
    NOT (`the first moment is before the second moment` (`the beginning of a day` `the day I am asking about`) (`the moment a provision commences on a day (s 15B)` `the day the law commences`))

-- s 18.  An Act or provision that expires on a day, or remains in force until a day, has effect until the end of the day.
@export Is a law still in force at the beginning of a given day if it expires on a day (s 18)?
GIVEN `the day the law expires or remains in force until` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the Act or provision expire, or until which day does it remain in force?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a law still in force at the beginning of a given day if it expires on a day` IF
    `the first moment is before the second moment` (`the beginning of a day` `the day I am asking about`) (`the last moment an Act or provision has effect (s 18)` `the day the law expires or remains in force until`)

-- s 20(2) and (4).  A repeal or amendment of an Act does not revive or affect a right, privilege or liability acquired,
-- accrued or incurred under the Act.  For any other thing these subsections do not say: NOTHING.
@export Does the repeal of an Act take away a right or liability I acquired under it (s 20)?
GIVEN `I acquired the right or privilege, or the liability accrued or was incurred, under the repealed or amended Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire a right or privilege under the Act, or did a liability accrue to you or get incurred by you under it, before it was repealed or amended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the repeal of an Act take away a right or liability I acquired under it` IS
    `the repeal or amendment of an Act revives or affects the thing (s 20(2) and (4))` `the thing`
    WHERE
        `the thing` MEANS
            IF `I acquired the right or privilege, or the liability accrued or was incurred, under the repealed or amended Act`
            THEN `a right, privilege or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the Act`
            ELSE `anything else`

-- s 20(3).  An investigation, proceeding or remedy relating to such a right, privilege, liability or penalty may be started,
-- continued or completed, and the right enforced or the penalty imposed, as if the repeal or amendment had not happened.
@export May I take a step about a right or penalty under a repealed Act as if it had not been repealed (s 20(3))?
GIVEN `it relates to a right, privilege, liability or penalty under the repealed or amended Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the step relate to a right, privilege or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the Act, or to a penalty incurred for an offence under it?
      step IS A `Step taken in relation to a repealed or amended Act` @desc What step do you want to take?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I take a step about a right or penalty under a repealed Act as if it had not been repealed` IS
    `the step may be taken as if the repeal or amendment had not happened (s 20(3))` step `it relates to a right, privilege, liability or penalty under the repealed or amended Act`

§§ `Counting my period: which day is my last day (s 38 and Schedule 1)`

-- s 38(1) and (2).  A period beginning on a given day, act or event is calculated by excluding that day; the day on which the
-- thing is to be done is included, so the last day of a period of n days is n days after the given day.
-- If that last day is an excluded day it is taken to fall on the next later day that is not an excluded day (s 38(2), (5)).
@export On which day does my period of days end (s 38(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `the day of the act or event` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the act or event happen from which your period runs (for example, the day the notice reached you)?
      `the number of days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days does the period give you?
      `I must file or register a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you must do to file or register a document?
      `the days my office is closed` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days after the period starts is the office where you must file or register closed? (leave empty if it is not a filing or registration)
      `the holidays where I must act` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days after the period starts are public holidays, special holidays or bank holidays in the place where you must act? (leave empty if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period of days end` IS
    `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))`
        `the day of the act or event`
        (`my period of days` `the number of days`)
        (`my purpose` `I must file or register a document`)
        (`the facts about my days` `the days my office is closed` `the holidays where I must act`)

-- s 38(1), (2) and Schedule 1 ("calendar month", "month").  A period of calendar months begins at the beginning of the day after the
-- given day, and each month ends immediately before the beginning of the corresponding day of the next month, or at the end of the next
-- month if there is no such day.
@export On which day does my period of months end (s 38(1) and (2), Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `the day of the act or event` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the act or event happen from which your period runs (for example, the day the notice reached you)?
      `the number of months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many calendar months does the period give you?
      `I must file or register a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you must do to file or register a document?
      `the days my office is closed` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days after the period starts is the office where you must file or register closed? (leave empty if it is not a filing or registration)
      `the holidays where I must act` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days after the period starts are public holidays, special holidays or bank holidays in the place where you must act? (leave empty if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period of months end` IS
    `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))`
        `the day of the act or event`
        (`my period of months` `the number of months`)
        (`my purpose` `I must file or register a document`)
        (`the facts about my days` `the days my office is closed` `the holidays where I must act`)

-- s 38(1), (2) and Schedule 1 ("calendar year", "year").  A period of years is read as twelve calendar months for each year.
@export On which day does my period of years end (s 38(1) and (2), Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `the day of the act or event` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the act or event happen from which your period runs (for example, the day the notice reached you)?
      `the number of years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years does the period give you?
      `I must file or register a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you must do to file or register a document?
      `the days my office is closed` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days after the period starts is the office where you must file or register closed? (leave empty if it is not a filing or registration)
      `the holidays where I must act` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days after the period starts are public holidays, special holidays or bank holidays in the place where you must act? (leave empty if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period of years end` IS
    `the day a period beginning on a given day ends once moved off an excluded day (s 38(1) and (2))`
        `the day of the act or event`
        (`my period of years` `the number of years`)
        (`my purpose` `I must file or register a document`)
        (`the facts about my days` `the days my office is closed` `the holidays where I must act`)

-- s 38(1)(a).  A period of a specified number of clear days, or at least a specified number of days, also excludes the day on which the
-- thing is to be done: the earliest day on which it can be done is the day after the last day counted.
-- The move off an excluded day in s 38(2) is not applied here: it speaks of the "last day" of a period.
@export On which day is the earliest I can act after a number of clear days (s 38(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the day of the act or event` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the act or event happen from which the clear days run?
      `the number of clear days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many clear days (or "at least" how many days) must pass?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day is the earliest I can act after a number of clear days` IS
    `the earliest day on which the purpose can be fulfilled after clear days (s 38(1)(a))` `the day of the act or event` `the number of clear days`

-- s 38(1).  The given day, act or event is excluded, so the day itself does not count; every later day does.
@export Does a day count in my period if the period begins on a given day (s 38(1))?
GIVEN `the day of the act or event` IS A DATE @desc On which day did the act or event happen from which your period runs?
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a day count in my period if the period begins on a given day` IF
    `a day is counted in a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` `the day of the act or event` `the day I am asking about`

-- s 38(1)(a) and (b).  The day on which the thing is to be done is not counted for clear days or at least a number of days;
-- in any other case it is counted.
@export Is the day on which I must act counted in my period (s 38(1))?
GIVEN `my period is expressed as clear days or as at least a number of days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your period expressed as a number of clear days, or as at least a number of days?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day on which I must act counted in my period` IS
    `the day on which the purpose is to be fulfilled is counted in the period (s 38(1)(a) and (b))` kind
    WHERE
        kind MEANS
            IF `my period is expressed as clear days or as at least a number of days`
            THEN `a specified number of clear days or at least a specified number of days`
            ELSE `any other period`

-- s 38(1) and (3).  A period calculated backwards from a given day also excludes that day; if the earliest day falls on an
-- excluded day it is taken to fall on the next earlier day that is not an excluded day.
@export On which day is the earliest I may act if I must act a number of days before a given day (s 38(1) and (3))?
GIVEN `the day the period is counted back from` IS A DATE @desc From which day is the period counted back (for example, the day of the hearing)?
      `the number of days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before that day?
      `I must file or register a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you must do to file or register a document?
      `the days my office is closed` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which days before that day is the office where you must file or register closed? (leave empty if it is not a filing or registration)
      `the holidays where I must act` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which days before that day are public holidays, special holidays or bank holidays in the place where you must act? (leave empty if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day is the earliest I may act if I must act a number of days before a given day` IS
    CONSIDER `the earliest day of a period of days calculated backwards from a given day (s 38(1) and (3))` `the day the period is counted back from` `the number of days`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST earliest THEN JUST (`the day a time or earliest day calculated backwards is taken to fall on (s 38(3))` earliest (`my purpose` `I must file or register a document`) (`the facts about my days` `the days my office is closed` `the holidays where I must act`))

-- s 38(5) and Schedule 1 ("business day").  For filing or registering a document, an excluded day is a day on which the office is
-- closed; otherwise it is a day that is not a business day, that is a Saturday, a Sunday, or a public, special or bank holiday in the place.
@export Is a given day a day that does not count when my last day falls on it (s 38(5))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc Which day are you asking about?
      `I must file or register a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing you must do to file or register a document?
      `the office is closed on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the office where you must file or register closed on that day?
      `it is a public holiday, special holiday or bank holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that day a public holiday, special holiday or bank holiday in the place where you must act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a given day a day that does not count when my last day falls on it` IF
    `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` `the day` (`my purpose` `I must file or register a document`)
        (`the facts about my days` closed holidays)
    WHERE
        closed MEANS IF `the office is closed on that day` THEN LIST `the day` ELSE EMPTY
        holidays MEANS IF `it is a public holiday, special holiday or bank holiday` THEN LIST `the day` ELSE EMPTY

-- s 38(4).  If no time is provided or allowed for doing a thing, it is to be done as soon as possible, and as often as the occasion happens.
-- When a time is provided, this subsection does not apply: NOTHING.
@export Must I act as soon as possible because no time is set (s 38(4))?
GIVEN `a time is provided or allowed for doing the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act or instrument provide or allow a time for doing the thing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I act as soon as possible because no time is set` IS
    CONSIDER `when a thing is to be done if no time is provided (s 38(4))` `a time is provided or allowed for doing the thing`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST when THEN JUST TRUE

§§ `Age and adulthood (s 38A and Schedule 1)`

-- s 38A.  A person is an age in years at the beginning of the person's birthday for the age.
-- A person born on 29 February has no birthday on 28 February of a year without a 29 February on one reading and has on another: NOTHING for that day.
@export How old am I on a given day (s 38A)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On which day do you want your age?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How old am I on a given day` IS
    `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` `my date of birth` `the day`

-- Schedule 1, "adult": an individual who is 18 or more.
@export Am I an adult on a given day (s 38A, Schedule 1)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc On which day do you want to know?
      `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual (a natural person, not a company or other body)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an adult on a given day` IS
    CONSIDER `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` `my date of birth` `the day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST age THEN `the person is an adult (Schedule 1, definition adult)` `I am an individual` age

§§ `Serving documents, and when a posted letter counts (Part 10)`

-- s 39(1).  A document that an Act requires or permits to be served on a person may be served in the ways the subsection lists.
-- A way it does not list is not answered by the subsection: NOTHING.
@export May a document be served on a person in a given way (s 39(1))?
GIVEN `an Act requires or permits the document to be served on a person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act require or permit the document to be served on the person?
      person IS A `Person served` @desc Is the person to be served an individual or a body corporate?
      way IS A `Way of serving a document` @desc In which way do you want to serve the document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May a document be served on a person in a given way` IS
    `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` `an Act requires or permits the document to be served on a person` person way

-- s 39A(1)(a).  Service by post may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting the document as a letter.
@export Is service by post effected by posting my document as a letter (s 39A(1))?
GIVEN `the document is properly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document properly addressed?
      `the document is prepaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the postage prepaid?
      `the document is posted as a letter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document posted as a letter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is service by post effected by posting my document as a letter` IS
    `service by post may be effected (s 39A(1)(a))` `the document is properly addressed` `the document is prepaid` `the document is posted as a letter`

-- s 39A(1)(b).  Service by post is taken to have been effected at the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course
-- of post, unless the contrary is proved.  When the contrary is proved the Act gives no time: NOTHING.
-- Whether that time is on or before the end of the last day is worked out by comparing the two moments.
@export Is my posted letter taken to have been served by the end of my last day (s 39A(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the day the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc On which day would the letter be delivered in the ordinary course of post?
      `the seconds after the beginning of that day` IS A NUMBER @desc At what time would it be delivered, in seconds after the beginning of that day? (for example, 9 am is 32400)
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that the letter was served at a different time?
      `my last day for service` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which the document may be served?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my posted letter taken to have been served by the end of my last day` IS
    CONSIDER `the time service by post is taken to have been effected (s 39A(1)(b))` delivery `the contrary is proved`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST effected THEN JUST (NOT (`the first moment is before the second moment` (`midnight of a day, the point of time at which the day ends (Schedule 1)` `my last day for service`) effected))
    WHERE
        delivery MEANS `Moment in a day` WITH
            `the calendar day` IS `the day the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`
            `seconds after the beginning of that calendar day` IS `the seconds after the beginning of that day`

§§ `Forms, verification and fee units (Parts 12A, 12B and 13)`

-- s 48A(1).  If a form is prescribed or approved under an Act, strict compliance with the form is not necessary, and substantial compliance is sufficient.
@export Is it enough that my form substantially complies with the prescribed form (s 48A(1))?
GIVEN `a form is prescribed or approved under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form prescribed or approved under an Act?
      `my compliance with the form is substantial` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your form comply substantially with the form?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it enough that my form substantially complies with the prescribed form` IS
    `substantial compliance with the form is sufficient (s 48A(1))` `a form is prescribed or approved under an Act` `my compliance with the form is substantial`

-- s 48A(2).  A form that requires it to be completed in a specified way, or specified information or documents to be included, or to be verified in a
-- specified way, is not properly completed unless the requirement is complied with.
@export Is my form properly completed if the form's requirement is not complied with (s 48A(2))?
GIVEN `the form has a requirement about how it is completed, what is included, or how it is verified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the form require it to be completed in a specified way, or specified information or documents to be included, attached or given with it, or it or its contents to be verified in a specified way?
      `I have complied with that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you complied with that requirement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my form properly completed if the form's requirement is not complied with` IS
    `the form is properly completed (s 48A(2))` `the form has a requirement about how it is completed, what is included, or how it is verified` `I have complied with that requirement`

-- s 49.  If an Act requires a document to be verified in a specified way, the purpose is not fulfilled unless the requirement is satisfied.
@export Is the purpose fulfilled if the verification the Act requires is not satisfied (s 49)?
GIVEN `an Act requires the document, or what is included with it, to be verified in a specified way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act require the document, or information or a document included in, attached to or given with it, to be verified in a specified way?
      `the verification requirement is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that requirement satisfied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the purpose fulfilled if the verification the Act requires is not satisfied` IS
    `the purpose is fulfilled (s 49)` `an Act requires the document, or what is included with it, to be verified in a specified way` `the verification requirement is satisfied`

-- s 48B(4) and s 48C(3).  The value of a fee unit for an Act is the amount a regulation prescribes for it, or $1 if none is prescribed.
-- The amount of a fee in dollars is the value of a fee unit times the number of fee units, rounded to the nearest cent (one-half upwards)
-- unless the Act provides its own way of rounding, which this question does not cover: NOTHING.
@export How many dollars is a fee expressed in fee units (s 48B(4), s 48C(3))?
GIVEN `the number of fee units` IS A NUMBER @desc How many fee units is the fee?
      `a regulation prescribes the value of a fee unit for the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a regulation prescribed the value of a fee unit for the Act under which the fee is payable?
      `the prescribed value of a fee unit in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What value in dollars does the regulation prescribe for a fee unit? (any number if none is prescribed)
      `the Act provides its own way of rounding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act under which the fee is payable provide its own way of rounding the amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many dollars is a fee expressed in fee units` IS
    IF `the Act provides its own way of rounding`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the amount of the fee or other matter in dollars (s 48C(3))` (`the value of a fee unit for an Act (s 48B(4))` prescribed) `the number of fee units` NOTHING)
    WHERE
        prescribed MEANS
            IF `a regulation prescribes the value of a fee unit for the Act`
            THEN JUST `the prescribed value of a fee unit in dollars`
            ELSE NOTHING
